At equilibrium all the energy is kinetic:
\[
\frac{1}{2}mv_{\max}^2=\frac{1}{2}kA^2
\]
\[
v_{\max}=A\sqrt{\frac{k}{m}}
=0.15\sqrt{\frac{64}{0.25}}
=2.4\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}
\]

The potential energy fraction is
\[
\frac{U_s}{E}=
\frac{\frac{1}{2}kx^2}{\frac{1}{2}kA^2}
=\frac{x^2}{A^2}
\]
At \(x=A/2\),
\[
\frac{U_s}{E}=\frac{1}{4}
\]

At equilibrium,
\[
E=\frac{1}{2}mv_{\max}^2
\]
so
\[
v_{\max}=\sqrt{\frac{2E}{m}}
=\sqrt{\frac{2(3.6)}{0.80}}
=3.0\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}
\]
